    "title": "Height over the palms",
    "p1": "Jebel Zagora is the mountain that gives the town its backdrop. A climb rewards you with views over the palm grove, ksars and the first sense of open desert beyond.",
    "p2": "Start early: heat builds fast and the light is better at the edges of the day. Carry water, wear sturdy shoes and do not underestimate the sun.",
    "p3": "It is a viewpoint hike more than a technical climb — still demanding in summer heat."
